$b['The Dual Wolf'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: The Dual Wolf - a powerful wolf whose anatomy transitions between fire and ice. One side has flowing ember-like fur, glowing cracks, and smoky tendrils. The other side has crystalline fur, frost-covered whiskers, and translucent ice structures. The transition must follow the wolf''s actual anatomy rather than creating an arbitrary split down the middle. The eyes should feel like two expressions of the same intelligent creature. An Elemental Fusion tattoo in black-and-grey realism. No text, labels, logos or watermarks in the tattoo. In the right panel it is on a man, outer upper arm, a medium-to-large tattoo that still sits well inside that area, not a full sleeve.'
